# Generated key material and built artifacts are not committed.
#
# The PKI is regenerated by ./make-pki.sh (2-tier) and ./make-pki-tiered.sh (3-tier),
# and the utilities by ./build.sh. Only the OpenSSL configurations under pki/ are
# source. Committing certificates without their keys, or keys at all, would leave a
# clone whose idempotence guard skips regeneration and whose flow cannot then run.

# generated certificates, keys, requests
pki/**/*.crt
pki/**/*.key
pki/**/*.csr
pki/**/*.srl
pki/**/*.pem

# built utilities and signed test clients
bin/

# keychains, PKCS#12 archives, pinned-requirement records, log captures
work/